ote", "bold": true}]}, {"id": "body-12491-textbox1-00002", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "For the appropriate management of STIs/RTIs syndrome, drugs in the watch group (azithromycin, cefixime and ceftriaxone) are the standard recommended for use as a first line treatment for the most STIs/RTIs starting at the Dispensary level, therefore, should be used only for STIs/RTIs at Primary HFs)", "runs": [{"text": "For"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "appropriate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "management"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "STIs/RTIs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "syndrome,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "drugs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "watch"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "group"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(azithromycin,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cefixime"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ceftriaxone) are the standard recommended for use as a first line treatment for the most STIs/RTIs starting at the Dispensary level, therefore, should be used only for STIs/RTIs at Primary HFs)"}]}, {"id": "body-12493", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Flow Chart 12.1: Management of Urethral Discharge Syndrome (UDS)", "runs": [{"text": "Flow", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Chart", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "12.1:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Management", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "of", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Urethral", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Discharge", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Syndrome", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "(UDS)", "bold": true}]}, {"id": "body-12496", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "", "runs": [], "images": [{"src": "/data/images/image15.jpeg", "alt": "image15.jpe